      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-15fd931b7867",
          "exact": "In this context, the term high dynamic range means there is a large amount of variation in light levels within a scene or an image. The dynamic range refers to the range of luminosity between the brightest area and the darkest area of that scene or image."
        }
      ],
      "observations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-15fd931b7867",
          "subject": "high dynamic range / dynamic range",
          "predicate": "defined as",
          "object": "large amount of variation in light levels within a scene or image; range of luminosity between the brightest and darkest area of that scene or image",
          "qualifiers": {
            "definitional": true,
            "both_terms_covered": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "EVD-001",
        "VAL-001",
        "VAL-002"
      ],
      "rationale": "引文原句与 claim 逐项对应：'high dynamic range means there is a large amount of variation in light levels within a scene or an image' 对应 claim 的'HDR（高动态范围）指场景或图像中光线水平变化大'；'The dynamic range refers to the range of luminosity between the brightest area and the darkest area of that scene or image' 对应 claim 的'动态范围指场景或图像中最亮区与最暗区之间的亮度范围'。语义转述无增删，两半句均被覆盖，无矛盾信息。",
